@node Controlling Echo
@subsection Character@comma{} Word And Line Echo.

@cindex line echo

@cindex character echo

@cindex word echo

By default@comma{} Emacsvox speaks characters as they are typed  @MDash{}
this is called character echo; Words are spoken as they are completed
 @MDash{} this is called word echo.  Emacsvox can also optionally
speak each line as it is typed  @MDash{} this is called line echo.

Character@comma{} word and line echo can be toggled  @MDash{} either in the
current buffer  @MDash{} or for all buffers (globally).  To toggle the
specific echo functionality for all buffers@comma{} precede the specific
command with @kbd{C-u}.  Note that in the documentation below@comma{} this
use of @kbd{C-u} is indicated using the common Emacs terminology of
@strong{prefix arg} or @strong{interactive prefix arg}.

@table @kbd
@item C-e d k
@findex emacsvox-toggle-character-echo

@kindex C-e d k

@code{emacsvox-toggle-character-echo}

Toggle state of Emacsvox character echo.  Interactive PREFIX arg
means toggle the global default value@comma{} and then set the current local
value to the result.
@item C-e d w
@findex emacsvox-toggle-word-echo

@kindex C-e d w

@code{emacsvox-toggle-word-echo}

Toggle state of Emacsvox word echo.  Interactive PREFIX arg means
toggle the global default value@comma{} and then set the current local value
to the result.
@item C-e d l
@findex emacsvox-toggle-line-echo

@kindex C-e d l

@code{emacsvox-toggle-line-echo}

Toggle state of Emacsvox line echo.  Interactive PREFIX arg means
toggle the global default value@comma{} and then set the current local value
to the result.
@end table

@node Speech Output Control
@subsection Setting  TTS Characteristics.

Emacsvox user commands can set different characteristics of the speech
output such as speech rate and  punctuations mode.

Emacsvox provides settings that affect how text attributes such as
capitalization and indentation are conveyed.  Each feature has a master
switch and a separately selected presentation@comma{} so enabling the feature does
not force one fixed sound.
These settings can be made locally in a given buffer or be applied to
all buffers by preceding these commands with @kbd{C-u}.

@table @kbd
@item C-e d r
@findex tts-set-rate

@kindex C-e d r

@code{tts-set-rate}

Set speaking RATE for the @acronym{TTS}.  Interactive PREFIX arg means set the
global default value@comma{} and then set the current local value to the
result.
@item C-e d f
@findex tts-set-character-scale

@kindex C-e d f

@code{tts-set-character-scale}

Set scale FACTOR for speech rate.  Speech rate is scaled by this
factor when speaking characters.  Interactive PREFIX arg means set the
global default value@comma{} and then set the current local value to the
result.
@item C-e d DIGIT
@findex tts-set-predefined-rate

@kindex C-e d DIGIT

@code{tts-set-predefined-rate}

Set speech rate to one of nine predefined levels using digit keys
@kbd{0} through @kbd{9}.  Interactive PREFIX arg says to set the rate
globally.
@item C-e d p
@findex tts-set-punctuations

@kindex C-e d p

@code{tts-set-punctuations}

Set punctuation mode to MODE@.  Possible values are @code{some}@comma{} @code{all}@comma{}
or @code{none}.  Interactive PREFIX arg means set the global default value@comma{}
and then set the current local value to the result.
@item C-e d s
@findex tts-toggle-split-caps

@kindex C-e d s

@code{tts-toggle-split-caps}

Toggle split caps mode.  Split caps mode is useful when reading
Hungarian notation in program source code.  Interactive PREFIX arg
means toggle the global default value@comma{} and then set the current local
value to the result.
@item C-e d c
@kindex C-e d c

@findex tts-toggle-caps

@code{tts-toggle-caps}

Toggle capitalization indication.  Interactive PREFIX arg means toggle the
global default value@comma{} then set the current local value to the result.
@item C-e d C
@kindex C-e d C

@findex emacsvox-set-capitalization-presentation

@code{emacsvox-set-capitalization-presentation}

Choose @code{spoken}@comma{} @code{tone}@comma{} @code{spoken-tone}@comma{} @code{custom}@comma{} or
@code{none}@comma{} and preview representative text.  @code{custom} publishes facts
for personal Aural Presentation rules without adding built-in output.  A
current Omnivox server applies the selected capitalization presentation to
isolated letters as well as queued words; older speech servers retain their
engine-specific isolated-letter behavior.
@end table

In addition@comma{} Emacsvox can convey the indentation of lines as they are
spoken  @MDash{} This is relevant when programming and is the default
when working with program source.

@table @kbd
@item C-e d i
@findex emacsvox-toggle-audio-indentation

@kindex C-e d i

@code{emacsvox-toggle-audio-indentation}

Toggle state of Emacsvox audio indentation.  Interactive PREFIX arg
means toggle the global default value@comma{} and then set the current local
value to the result.
@item C-e d I
@findex emacsvox-set-indentation-presentation

@kindex C-e d I

@code{emacsvox-set-indentation-presentation}

Choose spoken column@comma{} duration-coded tone@comma{} rising-pitch tone@comma{} either tone
combined with speech@comma{} @code{custom}@comma{} or @code{none}.  The command previews a
four-column indentation sample.  Indentation tones complete before the line is
