@chapter Manual Provenance And Contributions

This manual began as the second-edition Emacspeak user manual and still
contains selected chapters from that project.  Emacsvox-specific operating
guidance@comma{} names@comma{} requirements@comma{} and generated command reference are maintained
in this repository.  Historical chapters retain Emacspeak terminology where
that identity and period context matter.

@menu
* Contributing::
* Authoring Guidelines::
* Credits::
@end menu

@node Contributing
@section How To Contribute To This Manual

The maintained Org chapters live under @code{docs/manual/chapters/}; the current
project overview and installation summary live in @code{Readme.org} and
@code{etc/install.org}.
Submit changes through the Emacsvox repository at
@uref{https://github.com/bartbunting/emacsvox}.  Read @code{AGENTS.md} before
building or testing: Emacsvox requires Emacs 31 or newer and repository-local
@code{local.mk} selects the compiler used by supported targets.

Do not hand-edit generated references.  @code{info/docs.texi} and
@code{info/keys.texi} come from the source documentation generator;
@code{etc/aural-presentation-reference.org} comes from
@code{utils/emacsvox-aural-audit.el}.
The first two sources form the separately installed
@code{emacsvox-reference.info} manual.
The selected historical chapters form the separately installed
@code{emacsvox-heritage.info} manual.

@node Authoring Guidelines
@section Authoring Guidelines

Keep current operating instructions separate from historical accounts.  State
which back end or platform a procedure applies to@comma{} avoid duplicating detailed
protocol contracts across repositories@comma{} and link to the owning document.

Reports and internal notes require no Emacsvox build.  While editing the Org
manual@comma{} preview the complete user manual without inspecting or rebuilding Lisp
byte-code:

@example
make docs-org-preview
@end example

The ignored Info@comma{} Texinfo@comma{} and HTML previews appear under
@code{.docs-preview/org-manual/}.  Once the text settles@comma{} run
@code{make docs-update} to update the tracked generated Texinfo body and checked
Info files.  Do not edit those generated files directly.

When public Lisp documentation or keys change@comma{} first bring byte-code current
with @code{make bytecode}.  Use @code{make bytecode-rebuild} instead after
changing macros or public interfaces@comma{} as described in @code{AGENTS.md}.  Then
run @code{make docs-reference}.  @code{make docs-generate} remains the
comprehensive reference and manual update.  Before review@comma{} merge@comma{} or
deployment@comma{} run the non-mutating
@code{make docs-release-check}; @code{make docs-check} is its
compatibility alias.  Commit the regenerated @code{emacsvox.info}@comma{}
@code{emacsvox-reference.info}@comma{} and @code{emacsvox-heritage.info} files with
their source changes.

@subsection Publishing The Browser Manual

Org on @code{master} is the canonical maintained manual source.  GitHub Pages serves
the generated static files committed on the separate @code{gh-pages} branch;
never edit those HTML files as source.  Publishing is deliberately explicit:

@enumerate
@item
Finish the manual change@comma{} update its checked Info output@comma{} run the release
validation target above@comma{} and commit the complete source-side change on
@code{master}.

@item
Check out that exact commit in a clean source worktree.  Build its local@comma{}
ignored byte-code with the Emacs selected by @code{local.mk} or an
@code{EMACS=} override.  Use a separate sibling worktree checked out on
@code{gh-pages} as the publication directory.

@item
From the clean source worktree@comma{} run:

@example
make docs-publish-pages DOCS_PUBLISH_DIR=/path/to/emacsvox-pages
@end example

The target validates the manual and publishes that same staged render@comma{} replaces
only its managed HTML files@comma{} writes @code{.nojekyll}@comma{} and records the source
commit@comma{} Emacs version@comma{} and Texinfo version in @code{emacsvox-source.txt}.  It
refuses an uncommitted source tree.

@item
Inspect the @code{gh-pages} worktree@comma{} including the provenance file and the
main browser entry points.  Commit the generated site with the source commit
in the commit message@comma{} then push @code{master} and @code{gh-pages}.  The GitHub
Pages source setting must name the root of @code{gh-pages}.
@end enumerate

No documentation target creates a commit or pushes a branch.  This keeps the
published bytes reviewable and makes publication a distinct maintainer action.

